Q1. When MPS sends back a Follow-up Date, should the task still complete, or go into
    Follow-Up status instead?
    Context   : Every MPS callback completes the task today, and completion sets
                isFollowUp = 0. The screen hides the follow-up date on a completed task.
    Suggested : Keep completing the task as today and only save the date. The story
                says "Follow-up Date is updated in the source system" and asks for no
                status change. Moving the task into Follow-Up would be a new status
                transition and would leave it locked on the screen (MPSExtractDate).
    Impact    : Blocks the whole inbound Follow-up Date design (AC 5d).
    Status    : ⏳ Pending

Q2. In what format does MPS expect Payment Status outbound?
    Context   : Stored as 'P' / 'D' / NULL. The mapping image asks for "Number 1".
    Suggested : Send a number that mirrors the inbound paymentCode: P -> 1, D -> 0,
                NULL -> not sent. Both directions then mean the same thing.
    Impact    : Blocks the outbound Payment Status mapping and the DTO type.
    Status    : ⏳ Pending

Q3. What are the agreed JSON names and formats for the new fields?
    Context   : The names are a contract with MPS / Common Services.
    Suggested : Reuse the names the inbound contract already has, so both directions
                match: billNumber, penaltiesAndInterest, paymentCode, plus a new
                followUpDate (outbound and inbound).
                  - penaltiesAndInterest: decimal with 2 places, like amountDue.
                  - followUpDate outbound: sent the same way as the existing asofDate
                    and goodThruDate.
                  - followUpDate inbound: read with the existing lenient date parser,
                    which accepts YYYYMMDD and ISO.
                  - Empty values: sent as null, like the existing optional fields.
                This still needs MPS confirmation before merge.
    Impact    : Blocks the DTO changes in both directions.
    Status    : ⏳ Pending

Q4. Which P&I value goes in the outbound payload?
    Context   : The payload is one item per task; P&I is stored per installment in
                tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_YearInfo.
    Suggested : The P&I of the task's own tax year + installment. No value when that
                row does not exist (not 0, so MPS can tell "none" from "zero").
                Needs a new LASOutsourcing synonym and EF entity for Tax_YearInfo.
    Impact    : Blocks the new join and the synonym / EF entity design.
    Status    : ⏳ Pending

Q5. Which Bill Number goes outbound, and what happens when it is longer than 10?
    Context   : Bill Number exists per task (Tax_Info) and per installment
                (Tax_YearInfo). The column allows 50; DEV has nothing over 10.
    Suggested : Use tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_Info.BillNumber. If it is longer than 10,
                truncate to 10 and log the lengths (the existing mailing-address
                pattern), so the item is never dead-lettered (AC 3).
    Impact    : Blocks the outbound Bill Number mapping and its validation attribute.
    Status    : ⏳ Pending

Q6. Are AC 5a-5c considered met by the existing inbound handling?
    Context   : billNumber, penaltiesAndInterest and paymentCode are already received
                and saved for DIR / DMU.
    Suggested : Yes. No code change for these three; cover them with verification
                tests. Leave the two existing behaviours alone (an empty inbound bill
                number blanks the per-installment value; over-10 values are accepted),
                since changing them is outside this story.
    Impact    : Decides whether inbound work is Follow-up Date only.
    Status    : ⏳ Pending
