**Q10. What payload structure will MPS send back to us for an EPQ item? Is the sample below correct?** (MPS / Common Services)

- **Context:** when MPS finishes an EPQ item (DIR or DMU), it posts the result to our `POST /api/Receiver` endpoint. The story needs four values to come back. Three of them already exist in the message, and we plan to keep using those fields. Only Follow-up Date is new.

| Story field | Field in the message | Where | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bill Number | `billNumber` | inside each `taxLines` entry | Existing, reused as is |
| P&I | `penaltiesAndInterest` | inside each `taxLines` entry | Existing, reused as is |
| Payment Status | `paymentCode` (0 = unpaid, 1 = paid) | inside each `taxLines` entry | Existing, reused as is |
| Follow-up Date | `followUpDate` | top level of the message | **NEW, proposed** |

- **Suggested:** no change to the existing structure. Add one field, `followUpDate`, at the top level, because the follow-up date belongs to the whole item and not to one installment.

```jsonc
{
  "correlationId": "8addc3bb-2404-4dcb-baa3-e6b0eb54a523",
  "sourceUniqueId": "DMU-131397-45",
  "followUpDate": "20261215",              // NEW: Follow-up Date (proposed)
  "taxLines": [
    {
      "year": "2022",
      "installment": "1",
      "paymentCode": 0,                    // EXISTING: used for Payment Status
      "penaltiesAndInterest": 308.21,      // EXISTING: used for P&I
      "billNumber": "1234567890",          // EXISTING: used for Bill Number
      "amountDue": 5970.06,
      "baseAmount": 5400.73,
      "goodThruDate": "2026-12-31",
      "goodThruDate2": null,
      "balanceDue2": 0,
      "specialCondition": "",
      "asOfDate": "2026-11-18",
      "checkType": null,
      "eldDate": "2022-11-01",
      "notes": "Example note",
      "leretaLiability": null,
      "paymentOptionIndicator": null
    }
  ]
}
```

  The `//` comments are only there to explain the sample; they are not part of the message. Fields without a comment are existing fields that this story does not touch. The values are examples only.

- **Please confirm for the three existing fields:**
  - Bill Number, P&I and Payment Status will keep arriving in `taxLines` as `billNumber`, `penaltiesAndInterest` and `paymentCode`, with no rename and no new fields for them;
  - `paymentCode` keeps its meaning: 0 = unpaid, 1 = paid.
- **Please confirm for the new field:**
  - its name and position: `followUpDate` at the top level, as shown, or inside each tax line;
  - its format: `YYYYMMDD` as in the story, or another date format;
  - what is sent when there is no follow-up date: `null`, or the field left out;
  - whether a message carrying a follow-up date means the item is finished, or that MPS is still working on it and will send another message later.
- **Impact:** blocks the inbound Follow-up Date change (AC 5d). The last point also decides Q1, whether the task is completed or moved to Follow-Up.
- **Status:** ⏳ Pending

